{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:sectional-curvature","title":"def:sectional-curvature","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.md","line":135,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex#def:sectional-curvature","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex","label":"def:sectional-curvature","line":246,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Sectional curvature]\n\\label{def:sectional-curvature}\n\n\\uses{def:riemann-curvature-tensor}\n\n\n\n\nFor a $2$-plane $P\\subset T_pM$ with orthonormal basis $\\{X,Y\\}$,\nits \\emph{sectional curvature} is\n\\[\n  K(P)=\\mathcal R(X,Y,X,Y).\n\\]\nPositive, negative, nonnegative, and nonpositive sectional curvature\nmean the corresponding inequality holds for every $2$-plane.\n\\end{definition}\n\nFor $X=X^i\\partial_i$ and $Y=Y^j\\partial_j$ spanning $P$,\n\\[\n  K(P)=R_{ijkl}X^iY^jX^kY^l.\n\\]\nThe sectional curvature is \\emph{constant} if this value is independent\nof $p$ and $P\\subset T_pM$.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Sectional curvature] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a73656374696f6e616c2d637572766174757265\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Ariemann-curvature-tensor\">↗ def:riemann-curvature-tensor</a> <p></p>For a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$2$\">$2$</span>-plane <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$P\\subset T_pM$\">$P\\subset T_pM$</span> with orthonormal basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ X,Y\\} $\">$\\{ X,Y\\} $</span>, its <em>sectional curvature</em> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  K(P)=\\mathcal R(X,Y,X,Y).  \\]\">\\[  K(P)=\\mathcal R(X,Y,X,Y).  \\]</span> Positive, negative, nonnegative, and nonpositive sectional curvature mean the corresponding inequality holds for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$2$\">$2$</span>-plane.  <p></p>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X=X^i\\partial _i$\">$X=X^i\\partial _i$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Y=Y^j\\partial _j$\">$Y=Y^j\\partial _j$</span> spanning <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$P$\">$P$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  K(P)=R_{ijkl}X^iY^jX^kY^l.  \\]\">\\[  K(P)=R_{ijkl}X^iY^jX^kY^l.  \\]</span> The sectional curvature is <em>constant</em> if this value is independent of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$P\\subset T_pM$\">$P\\subset T_pM$</span>.","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#Bianchi","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:constant-curvature-tensor","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor","title":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor","label":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:constant-curvature-tensor","title":"lem:constant-curvature-tensor","label":"lem:constant-curvature-tensor"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:curvature-operator","title":"def:curvature-operator","label":"def:curvature-operator"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:cu